course: dictionary
lesson: 15304
title: Word pieces
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: "sle" is not a word on its own. It is a piece of a longer word, like the start of «sleep» or the middle of «isle». A piece like this is called a fragment.
explain: You may meet a fragment when a word has been cut short, for example in a list, or when a typing mistake leaves letters out. Read the words around it to find the full word.
explain: Example: «Her coat has a torn sle where the arm joins.» The sentence is about an arm, so «sle» is probably the start of «sleeve». Check it: does sleeve fit the sentence? If it does, you have found the word.
fact: "sle" is a fragment, not an English word by itself.
fact: Longer words that start with «sle» include «sleep», «sled» and «sleeve».
fact: The fragment «sle» can also sit inside a word, as in «isle».
fact: A fragment can come from a word that has been cut short or from a typing mistake.
fact: Context helps: read the sentence and ask which full word would fit there.
exercise: Which full word starts with «sle» and is what you ride down a snowy hill? | isle | *sled | sleeve
exercise: Which word has «sle» in the middle and means a small island? | *isle | sleep | sleeve | sled
exercise: «Her coat has a torn sle where the arm joins.» Which full word fits? | sled | isle | sleep | *sleeve
test: Which word starts with «sle» and is what you do at night in bed? | sled | *sleep | sleeve
test: Can you find «sle» in the dictionary as a word on its own? | Yes, it means sleepy | Yes, it is a word for a snowy hill | *No, it is only a piece of a longer word
exam: A pupil sees «sle» in a typed list: sle, boat, tree. What should she do? | Ignore it and go on | *Read the clues around it and try to find the full word | Guess a random word | Write sle in the answer
